  "notes": "Clean security review of chunk skills-docs: no quantifiable, reproducible exploit in the 26 assigned files. Scope accounting (ACTION-REVIEW-SEC-004): nothing removed; all 26 files read in full; the 12 changelog.json files are history data only. Examined and rejected candidates: (1) merge-resolve allowed-tools widened with Bash(git merge *) and Bash(git commit --no-edit) (SKILL.md L7). The grant is active only while the skill runs, compound commands stay denied by the global gate, and the only extra exec surface (git merge -s <name> running git-merge-<name> from PATH, or repo hooks) needs an attacker-planted binary or hook that already executes on any commit. No boundary crossed, so no claim. (2) foreign-toolchain-pretag.js L49 interpolates args.buildCmd into an agent prompt as 'Run: ...', and config-ui-fidelity-gate.js / subsystem-grounding.js interpolate templates/renderHint/drivers/planRef. All args come from the invoking session, the same principal, so there is no injection boundary. (3) No secrets, tokens or payload logging in any changed line (LOG-004/005). skillroutine-create keeps its size-only token handling unchanged. Cross-chunk notes for the station: (a) railroad-review.js moves every lane/refuter/station branch from claude/railroad-* to claude-review/*. If cmd/worktrees/remove_agent_worktrees.sh treats only claude/* as agent branches, a claude-review/* branch counts as a 'non-claude' branch in its reachability gate. Then /close (close SKILL.md L23-33) could delete a claude/<session> branch whose unique commits survive only on a claude-review/* branch, which round cleanup deletes later. Not verifiable inside this chunk, and it is data-integrity rather than an exploit; the related cleanup-refusal defect is known (correctness-BLK-29-r1). (b) skillroutine-create L36 makes frontmatter 'origin: user' the provenance marker that the casual lockout keys on. Only prose ('never add it to shipped skills') protects shipped skills from a proposal-driven edit that stamps the marker and so bypasses the lockout. Whether smine-apply's lockout reads this marker from the pre-edit or the post-edit file lives in another chunk (cf. known correctness-MAJ-61-r1)."
